  "principles": [
    "One math implementation, thin interfaces; adapters own workflows rather than duplicate solvers",
    "One canonical geometry representation plus typed variants, immutable shared data and bounded copy-on-write",
    "All metrology measurements carry units, datum/frame, tolerance, source revision, confidence, and provenance",
    "Use source-revision keyed bounded 3D spatial caches; do not confuse drafting 2D R-tree with 3D nearest-neighbor search",
    "Memory budgets, cancellation, deterministic tie-breaks, finite inputs and stable ID mappings are acceptance gates",
    "Never bundle or rely on proprietary PolyWorks/GOM/Design X runtime code in the native core",
    "Do not mark planned consumers as integrated until that adapter has actual runtime tests"
  ],
